================================================================================
ARCHITECTURE CLARIFICATIONS
================================================================================

SCHEDULER (fcfs_scheduler_HPO.py / fcfs_optimized_HPO.py):
- Receives workflow submission from user
- Evaluates budget and deadline constraints
- Makes ALL resource allocation decisions:
  * On-prem: Uses available capacity
  * Reserved: Uses pre-allocated cloud instances
  * On-demand: Creates new cloud instances (if budget allows)
- Sends complete allocation to executor via HTTP POST

EXECUTOR (executor_HPO.py):
- Runs on dedicated instance (doesn't participate in computation)
- Receives workflow from scheduler via HTTP server (port 8089)
- Pushes workflow to Redis queue
- processQueueData() thread spawns execution thread
- Uses ONLY the IPs provided by scheduler
- For moldable: Requests more/fewer resources from scheduler

STEEP WORKFLOW ENGINE (steep_workflow.py, steep_actions_HPO.py):
- Parses workflow YAML
- Executes ForEach actions (workflow iterations)
- Calls service script (run_hpo.py) via subprocess
- Passes JSON arguments to service script
- Parses JSON output from service script

SERVICE SCRIPT (run_hpo.py):
- Routes to PlclRunnerHPO (on-prem) or CloudRunnerHPO (cloud)
- Receives JSON request with hosts, chains, epochs, hyperparameters
- Returns JSON result with updated hyperparameters and next_trials

RUNNERS (plcl_runner_HPO.py / cloud_runner_HPO_new.py):
- Set up Ray cluster on WORKERS (not executor)
- Run HPO pipeline (hpo_pipeline_verbose.py)
- Return results to service script

HPO PIPELINE (hpo_pipeline_verbose.py):
- Runs Ray Tune hyperparameter optimization
- Refines search space based on best config
- Calculates adaptive trial count (next_trials)
- Returns JSON with best config and next_trials

